' Library Management Application — Business Workflow Diagram
' Auto-split from library-management-business-workflow.puml
' Render this file individually to avoid HTTP header size limits

@startuml Business_Process_Sequence
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam titleFontSize 16

title Business Process Sequence Diagram\nComplete Library Management Run

actor "Schedule Trigger" as Schedule
participant "Library Management\nApplication" as App
database "Existing Database" as DB
participant "External Library\nSource" as Ext
participant "Aggregation &\nComparison" as Logic
participant "Recommendation\nEngine" as Rec
participant "Email Service" as Email
participant "Teams Service" as Teams
actor "Recipients" as Users

== Step 1: Read Existing Library Information ==
Schedule -> App : Trigger regular run
App -> DB : Retrieve library records
DB --> App : Version + Information Notes\n(per library)

== Step 2: Pull Latest Library Information ==
loop For each library
  App -> Ext : Pull/Scrape latest version
  Ext --> App : Latest Version
  App -> Ext : Pull/Scrape release notes
  Ext --> App : Release Notes
end

== Step 3 & 4: Aggregation and Comparison ==
App -> Logic : Send DB data + External data
Logic -> Logic : Aggregate per library
Logic -> Logic : Compare DB version vs Latest version
Logic --> App : Comparison results\n(New version released: Y/N)

== Step 5: Recommendation Generation ==
App -> Rec : Send comparison results\n+ release notes + info notes
Rec -> Rec : Assess: Upgrade or Existing sufficient?
Rec -> Rec : Generate pros/cons for upgrade
Rec -> Rec : Generate pros/cons for no-upgrade
Rec --> App : Recommendation content

== Step 6: Email Notification ==
App -> Email : Send recommendation content
Email -> Users : Deliver email notification
Email --> App : Delivery status

== Step 7: Teams Notification ==
App -> Teams : Post recommendation content
Teams -> Users : Deliver Teams group message
Teams --> App : Post status

App -> Schedule : Update next run schedule

@enduml
